<title>SPAIN: Stability pact complements convergence - Spain Rato.</title>
<headline>Stability pact complements convergence - Spain Rato.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stability pact intended to keep fiscal discipline once the European single currency project is launched represents the continuation of Spain's convergence plan, Economy Ministry Rodrigo Rato said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;For Spain, the stability pact is a complement to the convergence programme, necessary to put an end to inflationary expectations,&quot;  Rato said in Frankfurt at a European banking congress, according to a statement from the Ministry.</p>
<p>According to Rato, the plan ensures the search for efficiency and competitiveness in European economies becomes a permanent challenge.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
